    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d645">

                <pb facs="0617" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg533"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860c.48/59</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Joint Distribution Committee
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Department regrets to inform you
                    that it has received unfavorable replies from the American Legations at The
                    Hague, Berne, Copenhagen and Stockholm, regarding the forwarding from those
                    countries to Poland, of clothing purchased in Holland, Switzerland, Denmark and
                    Sweden, respectively,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d645-f1"/> In view of the scarcity of
                    clothing in those countries, there appears to be no immediate possibility of
                    obtaining the permission of the local authorities for the exportation of wearing
                    apparel to Poland.</p>
                <p>Your check for $15,000 is therefore returned herewith.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                        
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d645-f1" n="2" xml:id="d645-f1-content">
                <p>See Department’s telegram of Mar. 21, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg529">p. 529</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
